OROCHIMARU RESEARCH DIVISION
GENETIC MODIFICATION — WORKING NOTES
CLEARANCE: RESEARCH CADRE

Aim
To transplant desirable traits — bloodline limits above all — from donor tissue into a
host body, and eventually into Lord Orochimaru's own line of vessels. These notes track
the transplantation program's progress and failures.

Working Notes
- Kaguya-line skeletal tissue (Shikotsumyaku) remains the most-studied graft. Donor
  material is finite; the natural bearer's decline has closed the primary source. Preserve
  all remaining samples in the Zone C vault.
- Senju-line cells were incorporated into early subject batches to test regenerative
  potential. Most hosts reject the graft outright; a rare few tolerate it and exhibit
  accelerated healing. These survivors are of great interest.
- Rejection is the central obstacle. The host's own network treats grafted bloodline
  tissue as foreign and destroys it, or is destroyed by it. Immunosuppressive sealing
  reduces but does not eliminate this.

Standing Priorities
1. Stabilize a host that can carry a foreign kekkei genkai without rejection.
2. Expand the donor library (see collection log).
3. Feed viable results into the immortality archive and the body-transfer program.

Continue logging every batch, survivor and non-survivor alike.
